# ripgrep / fd ignore — GENERATED BUNDLES ONLY (EI-19448801536482587)
#
# This file is read by ripgrep and fd, NOT by git. It exists solely to keep
# multi-megabyte GENERATED build artifacts out of interactive search results.
# Nothing here is source, and nothing here is excluded from git by this file.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS — measured 2026-08-03:
#
#   papercusp-desktop/src-tauri/sidecar/serve.mjs             44,718,412 B
#   papercusp-desktop/src-tauri/env-sidecars/staging/serve.mjs 44,549,123 B
#   longest single line in each:                                3,965,335 B
#
# These are esbuild bundles that inline the whole of `operator-core`, minified
# onto a handful of ~4MB lines. `grep -n` prints the MATCHING LINE, so one hit
# inside a 4MB line dumps ~4MB into the caller's output. Because they inline
# operator-core, nearly any symbol an agent searches for is present in them, so
# this fires on ordinary searches rather than exotic ones.
#
# The concrete cost: a routine `grep -rn 'DEFAULT_CONTENT_DETECTORS'` (already
# scoped with --include and already excluding node_modules) returned ~15,000
# tokens of minified JS — roughly 4% of an agent's context window — to answer a
# question whose real answer was 9 short lines. The loss is silent and
# unrecoverable, and can push an agent into a compaction mid-task.
#
# Searching these is never what anyone wants: the source they were built from is
# in packages/operator-core/lib/** and matches the same query. The repo already
# treats them this way — ~12 lint guards (check-no-raw-setinterval,
# check-timer-classification, check-no-control-bytes, scan-retirement-surface, …)
# each hand-roll an `f.includes('/env-sidecars/')` skip. This file extends the
# same established exclusion to interactive search, which had no equivalent.
#
# NOTE ON COVERAGE — this fixes ripgrep/fd (and therefore agent Grep tooling),
# which is the common path. A raw `grep -rn` does NOT read .ignore files and is
# still exposed; prefer rg, or bound the damage with `-I` / --max-columns.

# Generated Tauri sidecar trees (esbuild bundles, vendored binaries, wasm blobs)
papercusp-desktop/src-tauri/sidecar/
papercusp-desktop/src-tauri/env-sidecars/

# Composed rig-VM sidecar — build OUTPUT (already gitignored; listed so a local
# build that predates that entry cannot leak into search either).
.rig-sidecar-current/
